    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q46-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\displaystyle \\binom{n}{k}=\\binom{n+1}{k+1}-\\binom{n}{k+1}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p40-q46-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\binom{n+1}{k+1}-\\binom{n}{k+1}=\\binom{n}{k}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p40-q46-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Write the right-hand side in factorial form and combine over a common denominator.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For $0\\leq k<n$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{n+1}{k+1}-\\binom{n}{k+1}&=\\frac{(n+1)!}{(k+1)!(n-k)!}-\\frac{n!}{(k+1)!(n-k-1)!}\\\\\\binom{n+1}{k+1}-\\binom{n}{k+1}&=\\frac{(n+1)n!-(n-k)n!}{(k+1)!(n-k)!}\\\\\\binom{n+1}{k+1}-\\binom{n}{k+1}&=\\frac{(k+1)n!}{(k+1)!(n-k)!}\\\\\\binom{n+1}{k+1}-\\binom{n}{k+1}&=\\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\\\\\\binom{n+1}{k+1}-\\binom{n}{k+1}&=\\binom{n}{k}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $k=n$, the right-hand side is $1-0=1=\\binom{n}{n}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q46-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that\n$$\\binom{k}{k}+\\binom{k+1}{k}+\\binom{k+2}{k}+\\cdots+\\binom{n}{k}=\\binom{n+1}{k+1}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p40-q46-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\displaystyle\\sum_{r=k}^{n}\\binom{r}{k}=\\binom{n+1}{k+1}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p40-q46-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use part (a); successive combination terms cancel.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Using part (a),\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sum_{r=k}^{n}\\binom{r}{k}&=1+\\sum_{r=k+1}^{n}\\left[\\binom{r+1}{k+1}-\\binom{r}{k+1}\\right]\\\\\\sum_{r=k}^{n}\\binom{r}{k}&=1+\\binom{n+1}{k+1}-\\binom{k+1}{k+1}\\\\\\sum_{r=k}^{n}\\binom{r}{k}&=\\binom{n+1}{k+1}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe intermediate terms cancel. When $n=k$, both sides equal $1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
